" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Plans for more Shards?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shards as in non-canonical settings for folks to have fun in, a la Dragon &amp; Masks?<br /> <br /> There are a few ideas in a pre-pitch stage. I don't know that I could call them plans at the moment, but there's a pitch in particular that's pretty likely to happen. I think a lot of folks will have fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T08:21:25-07:00","id":1464590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1464561#post1464561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shards as in non-canonical settings for folks to have fun in, a la Dragon &amp; Masks?<br /> <br /> There are a few ideas in a pre-pitch stage. I don't know that I could call them plans at the moment, but there's a pitch in particular that's pretty likely to happen. I think a lot of folks will have fun with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wonderful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T10:38:57-07:00","id":1464596,"title":"","content":"Does Saint and Monsters features minotaurs or Giants as player characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T13:10:19-07:00","id":1464626,"title":"","content":"Will there be rules for playing cthonians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T23:13:28-07:00","id":1464699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1464596#post1464596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Saint and Monsters features minotaurs or Giants as player characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been uninvolved in Saints &amp; Monsters' development, so that doesn't feel like my spoiler to give. I'll invite the dev to answer and see if they feel like answering, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T23:35:45-07:00","id":1464704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1464626#post1464626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be rules for playing cthonians?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in a how-to on running an Underworld?<br /> <br /> There's a <i>little</i> of that coming up soon in Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery. I don't know if a more in-depth look is feasible, as every Underworld is different. Heck, Mictl\u00e1n's actually 9 Underworlds (although most of the actual business takes place in Chiconahual\u00f3yan.) That's not a definite &quot;no,&quot; but it is something that'll be challenging to pull off.<br /> <br /> For right now, I don't have a solution that does a good enough job of walking the line between cultural respect, breadth of options, and playable content. If that changes, I think it'll make for a fun book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T11:22:14-07:00","id":1464892,"title":"","content":"No, I meant playing the actually creatures. Could you play a demon, or a Fury?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T17:33:14-07:00","id":1465067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1464892#post1464892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I meant playing the actually creatures. Could you play a demon, or a Fury?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totally. Those would both count as Denizens, which have rules at the end of Origin, starting on page 162. There are a few templates that I could see as appropriate for Erinyes out of the box, depending on which aspects you're interested in.<br /> <br /> Denizens are getting some love in Saints and Monsters, as seen here: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/scion-saints-monsters-preview-3/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/scion-saints-monsters-preview-3/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:25:41-07:00","id":1465077,"title":"","content":"does scion: god takes cues from other rpg's about playing godlike characters? like the jenna moran ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T01:53:55-07:00","id":1465488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1465077#post1465077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does scion: god takes cues from other rpg's about playing godlike characters? like the jenna moran ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's any direct cues from her, but I'm sure some of her work at least indirectly inspired some of the ideas. There are a lot of Exalted fans working on God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T03:40:28-07:00","id":1465996,"title":"","content":"Is Saints and Monsters getting kickstarted for a print run or going to pod on drivethru?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T05:44:43-07:00","id":1466116,"title":"","content":"Is there any plans to finish the origin and hero books with corrections, examples and working mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20788-burbankfr","name":"Burbankfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T07:58:10-07:00","id":1466287,"title":"","content":"Can you share any details on <i><b>No Gods, No Masters</b></i> (or point me in the direction of the relevant blog posts if I missed them)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:27:26-07:00","id":1466399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1465996#post1465996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Saints and Monsters getting kickstarted for a print run or going to pod on drivethru?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm about 80% sure that Saints and Monsters is going straight to PoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:31:02-07:00","id":1466401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burbankfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466116#post1466116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any plans to finish the origin and hero books with corrections, examples and working mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics work fine for me. Have you tried turning your books off and on again?<br /> <br /> On the off-chance that you're serious, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/274130/Scion-Second-Edition-Errata-and-FAQ\" target=\"_blank\">the errata book</a> may have the corrections you're looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T21:36:47-07:00","id":1466402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSM3050</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466287#post1466287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you share any details on <i><b>No Gods, No Masters</b></i> (or point me in the direction of the relevant blog posts if I missed them)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! The gist of No Gods, No Masters is that it's a pre-made campaign; it has a collection of linked adventures that center on the Keepers of the World. The Keepers are a group of Gods who were mistreated as mortals and, now that they're Gods, have an axe to grind. Imhotep \u2014 among others \u2014 have decided that the World will be better off without Gods. His goal is to cut the World off from the Pantheons and leave science and reason in charge of the humanity.<br /> <br /> Player Scions are free to fight the Keepers, join them, or find something even weirder to do with their time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T09:46:03-07:00","id":1466664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466401#post1466401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics work fine for me. Have you tried turning your books off and on again?<br /> <br /> On the off-chance that you're serious, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/274130/Scion-Second-Edition-Errata-and-FAQ\" target=\"_blank\">the errata book</a> may have the corrections you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does the Stun tag for weapons work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:20:11-07:00","id":1466686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466401#post1466401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics work fine for me. Have you tried turning your books off and on again?<br /> <br /> On the off-chance that you're serious, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/274130/Scion-Second-Edition-Errata-and-FAQ\" target=\"_blank\">the errata book</a> may have the corrections you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad the system is perfect for you, a developper of the game, but as someone who hasn't taken parts in the developpement process but has backed the original kickstarter and received the first print books and used the corrected pdf since, I still need to come on this forum and on the discord server to have clarifications.<br /> Since most answers I receive are &quot;These rules are clearer in Trinity&quot;, or &quot;This is a remnant from a rule that has been changed or that has disappeared but still exist in Trinity&quot;, and that a lot of post on these forums are questions for rule clarifications I don't think the books are quite done yet.<br /> <br /> You can see this post on the forum ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411256-honest-question-how-does-scion-2e-play\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-scion-2e-play</a> ) and the reviews on Drivethrurpg to get a sense of the numerous issues left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20788-burbankfr","user":"Burbankfr","date":". 11-04-2021, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20788-burbankfr","name":"Burbankfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T22:25:21-07:00","id":1466898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466664#post1466664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does the Stun tag for weapons work?</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sure. That\u2019s solid question caused by a combination of Storypath\u2019s open-ended handling of tags and a bit orphaned text.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The text of the Stun tag reads:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stun (1): When inflicting an Injury, this weapon can only be used to inflict the Minor Injury Conditions Bruised, Staggered, or Stunned, or the Major Injury Condition Battered. When a character is Taken Out by a weapon with the Stun tag, they are knocked unconscious.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> We basically have 2 problems here:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 What\u2019s a Minor or Major Injury Condition? &amp;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 What do those Conditions do?<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">First, Minor and Major Injury Conditions don\u2019t actually exist in the game. So, we don\u2019t know what the terms mean. Rather than worry about orphaned categories, we\u2019ll use the Injury Condition levels that are in the game (Bruised/Injured/Maimed). This gives us 4 Injury Conditions that we can slot into 3 categories.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Bruised: Definitely Bruised level</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Staggered: This doesn\u2019t sound like an injury, so it\u2019s also Bruised level</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Stunned: Probably Injured level.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Battered: Probably Maimed level.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Are these levels definitely correct? Not by RAW, but they work within the rules framework, so let\u2019s call it good and move to what they do.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Injury Conditions are deliberately open-ended, which allows Storyguides to add whatever they want. There are general guidelines in Origin (the levels are -1, -2, -4), and examples (a Black Eye is a Bruised-level Condition that adds +1 Difficulty to Firearms actions). This loose framework allows Storyguides to make things up on the spot, creating really niche Conditions, like Impaled by an Award Statuette (Maimed level) or Stepped on a Lego (Bruised level). This open-endedness is really helpful for Storyguides who\u2019re used to doing mechanical work on the fly, but sucks for folks who like concrete answers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So, to help folks who want more Injury Condition examples, here\u2019s some for the 3 undefined Injury Conditions for Stun weapons:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Staggered (-1 Defense as they try to shake it off/+1 Difficulty to actions using Agility)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Stunned (Limited to 1 reflexive action per turn &amp; cannot take mixed actions/+2 Difficulty to all Finesse actions)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Battered: (+4 Difficulty to all Finesse actions/Cannot take reflexive or mixed actions &amp; +4 Difficulty to movement)</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T22:30:25-07:00","id":1466899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burbankfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466686#post1466686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm glad the system is perfect for you, a developper of the game, but as someone who hasn't taken parts in the developpement process but has backed the original kickstarter and received the first print books and used the corrected pdf since, I still need to come on this forum and on the discord server to have clarifications.<br /> Since most answers I receive are &quot;These rules are clearer in Trinity&quot;, or &quot;This is a remnant from a rule that has been changed or that has disappeared but still exist in Trinity&quot;, and that a lot of post on these forums are questions for rule clarifications I don't think the books are quite done yet.<br /> <br /> You can see this post on the forum ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411256-honest-question-how-does-scion-2e-play\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-scion-2e-play</a> ) and the reviews on Drivethrurpg to get a sense of the numerous issues left.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I actually didn\u2019t join Team Scion until after after Origin and Hero were out and didn't become a developer for Scion until this year; I had to learn the system in much the same way that any other fan of the game did. I\u2019m NOT saying \u201cI can play the game, so everyone else can, too.\u201d I\u2019m saying that the flaws that you seem focused on aren\u2019t as big as you seem to think they are.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Do flaws exist? Sure. Everything ever published has its own problems. I don\u2019t think the ones in Origin and Hero are substantial enough that they require producing a new version, which is more of a headache than folks realize. So, to re-answer your original question, we\u2019re pretty unlikely to see an Origin or Hero 2.5.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That said, it seems like some of the problems you\u2019re having with the game are less with the rules and more to do with the rules presentation. That is something I can and will do something about. I\u2019m a former university lecturer, and making material more accessible is kind of my jam. I plan on putting out rules and setting info in more digestible forms, including videos. I don\u2019t have an ETA on those, but the first few will probably come out in the next few months.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T16:54:12-07:00","id":1466996,"title":"","content":"There is any plancto release a compendium of qualities and flairs for Scion? I think this would be great to quick create monsters and enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T17:04:54-07:00","id":1466999,"title":"","content":"Also i would like to ask if its intended the Transformation knack Power Tasting Bite ( From Scion Dragon manuscript), work on ranged attacks, its rules text only says \u201cyou need give damage\u201d,but it dont \u201cfeels right\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T20:59:38-08:00","id":1467324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466996#post1466996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is any plancto release a compendium of qualities and flairs for Scion? I think this would be great to quick create monsters and enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not right now, although I can certainly the potential in such a book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T21:18:38-08:00","id":1467325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466999#post1466999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also i would like to ask if its intended the Transformation knack Power Tasting Bite ( From Scion Dragon manuscript), work on ranged attacks, its rules text only says \u201cyou need give damage\u201d,but it dont \u201cfeels right\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that ranged attacks don't sound like tastes or bites, I can see a few cases where ranged attacks would feed directly into the flavor, such as a weapon with the returning tag or some sort of Dragon Magic that could deal damage and then flow back into you. I'm specifically envisioning using Fire Shaping to lash out at a foe, then pulling the fire back into yourself to &quot;taste&quot; the Flair.<br /> <br /> If I were Storyguiding, I'd ask a player who's trying to use it with a gun why they think it'd work; if they come up with a halfway plausible answer, I'd give it to them. I tend towards the rule of cool with Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T05:37:40-08:00","id":1467432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1466898#post1466898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\