00000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Staggered: This doesn\u2019t sound like an injury, so it\u2019s also Bruised level</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Stunned: Probably Injured level.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Battered: Probably Maimed level.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Are these levels definitely correct? Not by RAW, but they work within the rules framework, so let\u2019s call it good and move to what they do.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Injury Conditions are deliberately open-ended, which allows Storyguides to add whatever they want. There are general guidelines in Origin (the levels are -1, -2, -4), and examples (a Black Eye is a Bruised-level Condition that adds +1 Difficulty to Firearms actions). This loose framework allows Storyguides to make things up on the spot, creating really niche Conditions, like Impaled by an Award Statuette (Maimed level) or Stepped on a Lego (Bruised level). This open-endedness is really helpful for Storyguides who\u2019re used to doing mechanical work on the fly, but sucks for folks who like concrete answers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So, to help folks who want more Injury Condition examples, here\u2019s some for the 3 undefined Injury Conditions for Stun weapons:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Staggered (-1 Defense as they try to shake it off/+1 Difficulty to actions using Agility)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Stunned (Limited to 1 reflexive action per turn &amp; cannot take mixed actions/+2 Difficulty to all Finesse actions)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Battered: (+4 Difficulty to all Finesse actions/Cannot take reflexive or mixed actions &amp; +4 Difficulty to movement)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> If I'm reading correctly, shouldn't Stun be a 0pt tag then? It sounds you're saying it's just meant to be a flavor of damage that influences the injury conditions you'd apply. Basically an explicitly non-lethal companion to the Lethal (0) and Bashing (0) tags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T17:11:45-08:00","id":1467737,"title":"","content":"can you tell us more about how it feels to be a God in upcoming Scion: God? How do we get in that headspace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:36:22-08:00","id":1467961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1467432#post1467432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> If I'm reading correctly, shouldn't Stun be a 0pt tag then? It sounds you're saying it's just meant to be a flavor of damage that influences the injury conditions you'd apply. Basically an explicitly non-lethal companion to the Lethal (0) and Bashing (0) tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. The only way I can see it being worth a point is if Staggered, Stunned, and Battered are a little meaner than average. Revising the tag down to 0pt is probably the cleanest solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:39:18-08:00","id":1467962,"title":"","content":"Would you be able to tell us anything about the Zemi of the Taino or the pantheon from the Philippines whose name eludes me at the moment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22488-ventruestereotype","name":"VentrueStereotype","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T19:50:16-08:00","id":1467968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1467737#post1467737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you tell us more about how it feels to be a God in upcoming Scion: God? How do we get in that headspace?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Scion: God's set up to accommodate three basic modes.<br /> <br /> <b>1: Divine Rule:</b> If you want to hang out in an Overworld, Underworld, or other Realm and rule that place, you can do that. Working as a God has its own set of options. Like, you need to maintain your Mantles (or at least you should), but there are options for how to do that. A God could snap their fingers to raise a mountain to demonstrate their mastery, but they could also break out a shovel and do it by hand, work with another God, or perform a miracle. Divine Rule is also where you'd get into fights with other Gods and manage <br /> <br /> <b>2: Incarnations:</b> This <i>kind of</i> works like Hero, but with a very important difference: you're not just an Incarnate bumbling around The World; you're a God strategically creating Incarnations in order to accomplish something. Again, there are options within this. Like, you might be playing a game where everyone's character is an Incarnation of the same God! Or you might end up blurring the lines between Player and Storyguide because each Player is trying to change the nature of The World in some small fashion. Despite looking like previous games at first glance, there's actually a lot to do with Incarnations as a God.<br /> <br /> <b>3: Cults &amp; Religions:</b> Here, you feel the worship of mortals, but you also feel the need to fulfill at least some of their prayers or at least fend off other Gods or beliefs that are encroaching on your worshippers. And, as you might expect, Gods don't have a simple homogenous group of followers; cultists in S\u00e3o Paulo might have different views, ceremonies, and practices than your worshippers in NYC. So, tending to your followers can vary a fair bit. At a relatively core level, you're trying to take care of your followers and at least prevent their numbers from shrinking. Of course, you could also try to grow your religion, even splitting off from your Pantheon to try to become even bigger than any of your former family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T10:36:08-08:00","id":1468153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1467968#post1467968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Scion: God's set up to accommodate three basic modes.<br /> <br /> <b>1: Divine Rule:</b> If you want to hang out in an Overworld, Underworld, or other Realm and rule that place, you can do that. Working as a God has its own set of options. Like, you need to maintain your Mantles (or at least you should), but there are options for how to do that. A God could snap their fingers to raise a mountain to demonstrate their mastery, but they could also break out a shovel and do it by hand, work with another God, or perform a miracle. Divine Rule is also where you'd get into fights with other Gods and manage<br /> <br /> <b>2: Incarnations:</b> This <i>kind of</i> works like Hero, but with a very important difference: you're not just an Incarnate bumbling around The World; you're a God strategically creating Incarnations in order to accomplish something. Again, there are options within this. Like, you might be playing a game where everyone's character is an Incarnation of the same God! Or you might end up blurring the lines between Player and Storyguide because each Player is trying to change the nature of The World in some small fashion. Despite looking like previous games at first glance, there's actually a lot to do with Incarnations as a God.<br /> <br /> <b>3: Cults &amp; Religions:</b> Here, you feel the worship of mortals, but you also feel the need to fulfill at least some of their prayers or at least fend off other Gods or beliefs that are encroaching on your worshippers. And, as you might expect, Gods don't have a simple homogenous group of followers; cultists in S\u00e3o Paulo might have different views, ceremonies, and practices than your worshippers in NYC. So, tending to your followers can vary a fair bit. At a relatively core level, you're trying to take care of your followers and at least prevent their numbers from shrinking. Of course, you could also try to grow your religion, even splitting off from your Pantheon to try to become even bigger than any of your former family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! May I ask if the pantheon pages on God have info on how to interact with the figure there as a fully fledged God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:39:20-08:00","id":1468203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VentrueStereotype</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1467962#post1467962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you be able to tell us anything about the Zemi of the Taino or the pantheon from the Philippines whose name eludes me at the moment</div> </div> </div> </div>The Zem\u00ed take care of their people, much as shepherds take care of their flock. This is not unusual for Pantheons, but they take it to somewhat of an extreme. For millennia, they knew of the existence of non-Ta\u00edno people, but dismissed those humans as being irrelevant. Since the 15th century, they've been working to reshape their worldview, realizing that there are valuable allies and dangerous foes beyond their home islands.<br /> <br /> The Balahala represent the Visayan region of the Philippines and are comprised of both ancestral heroes that have risen to divinity and manifestations of nature. Like the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 and Loa, the Balahala don't take part in the Titanomachy because they don't see Titans (or Primordials for that matter) as being different from the Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T09:52:43-08:00","id":1468353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1467968#post1467968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Scion: God's set up to accommodate three basic modes.<br /> <br /> <b>1: Divine Rule:</b> If you want to hang out in an Overworld, Underworld, or other Realm and rule that place, you can do that. Working as a God has its own set of options. Like, you need to maintain your Mantles (or at least you should), but there are options for how to do that. A God could snap their fingers to raise a mountain to demonstrate their mastery, but they could also break out a shovel and do it by hand, work with another God, or perform a miracle. Divine Rule is also where you'd get into fights with other Gods and manage</div> </div> </div> </div> What would be the pros and cons of snap their fingers vs shovel a new mountain into being?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T05:17:53-08:00","id":1468392,"title":"","content":"<b>What Knack Skill roll really mean in Knacks section?</b> Is it roll on Skill dots alone, Skill + Calling or Skill + Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T00:09:27-08:00","id":1468461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1468153#post1468153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! May I ask if the pantheon pages on God have info on how to interact with the figure there as a fully fledged God?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, as that's going to be very open-ended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T00:15:15-08:00","id":1468462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1468353#post1468353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the pros and cons of snap their fingers vs shovel a new mountain into being?</div> </div> </div> </div>Snapping their fingers to make a mountain is going to cost a fair bit of Legend, and the mountain might not look exactly like what they want it to.<br /> Putting in the work is imbuing Legend to achieve the goal, which will look exactly like what they wanted, as they have control over it from start to finish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T00:31:46-08:00","id":1468464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1468392#post1468392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What Knack Skill roll really mean in Knacks section?</b> Is it roll on Skill dots alone, Skill + Calling or Skill + Attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin, p. 105<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:CrudFont\">KNACK SKILLS </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT\">Many Knacks reference Knack Skill rolls. The Storyguide and player choose the most appropriate Skill for each Knack. As usual, the Storyguide chooses the Arena for any Knack Skill roll, and the player chooses an Approach. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT\"><br /> tl;dr You and your SG figure out the Skill, your SG decides whether it's Mental, Physical, or Social, and you decide if your character's using Power, Finesse, or Resistance<br /> <br /> e.g. Dudeface McGee, Scion of Inari, wants to use the Heroic Creator Knack &quot;We Go All Night&quot; to build a sweet stereo system. The player and SG agree this is definitely Technology. The SG declares this a Mental task. The player argues that Dudeface is working smarter, not harder, and rolls using Cunning. So, Technology + Cunning. <br /> <br /> Had the SG declared it a Physical task, and Dudeface stuck with Finesse, it would have been Technology + Dexterity.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T07:28:46-08:00","id":1468498,"title":"","content":"S\u00f3 in Hero, the Player characters get fatebound to individuals <br /> In Demigod,they get Fatebound to groups of people,alongside realms and birthright and if they don't invoke the fatebinding,trouble arises.<br /> Can you give the generals on how Fate works on God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T13:02:59-08:00","id":1468627,"title":"","content":"Any talk among the devs to get dominion writeups for the PSPs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25904-nika777","name":"nika777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T22:27:00-08:00","id":1468660,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1467968#post1467968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Scion: God's set up to accommodate three basic modes.<br /> <br /> <b>2: Incarnations:</b> This <i>kind of</i> works like Hero, but with a very important difference: you're not just an Incarnate bumbling around The World; you're a God strategically creating Incarnations in order to accomplish something. Again, there are options within this. Like, you might be playing a game where everyone's character is an Incarnation of the same God! Or you might end up blurring the lines between Player and Storyguide because each Player is trying to change the nature of The World in some small fashion. Despite looking like previous games at first glance, there's actually a lot to do with Incarnations as a God.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Incarnations Origin level or can gods create Hero/Demigod level selves?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T23:44:32-08:00","id":1469149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1468498#post1468498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S\u00f3 in Hero, the Player characters get fatebound to individuals<br /> In Demigod,they get Fatebound to groups of people,alongside realms and birthright and if they don't invoke the fatebinding,trouble arises.<br /> Can you give the generals on how Fate works on God?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works more or less the same way, although there are a bunch of new ways to get Fatebound spinning off of each of the types of God-level play. You can even exceed your maximum number of Fatebindings, although doing so is not a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T23:47:28-08:00","id":1469150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nika777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1468627#post1468627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any talk among the devs to get dominion writeups for the PSPs?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's talk and a few ideas on how we want it to work. It's going to be a work in progress for a while, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T23:50:53-08:00","id":1469151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1468660#post1468660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are the Incarnations Origin level or can gods create Hero/Demigod level selves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods can Incarnate as Hero-tier, who can ascend to Demigod (which creates its own fun problems).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T23:54:49-08:00","id":1469152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469149#post1469149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works more or less the same way, although there are a bunch of new ways to get Fatebound spinning off of each of the types of God-level play. You can even exceed your maximum number of Fatebindings, although doing so is not a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Fatebounding for Gods to countries/nations even?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T09:41:16-08:00","id":1469405,"title":"","content":"Can you guys reveal any preliminary thoughts on how pantheon creation is going to go, for players who want to start their own faith seperate from the ones in the book? Mainly, is this going to be very freeform with guidelines on how to handle it at the table, or are there mechanics planned to attach to this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25904-nika777","user":"nika777","date":". 12-02-2021, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25904-nika777","name":"nika777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T09:41:46-08:00","id":1469406,"title":"","content":"Also, thanks so much for starting this thread. It's a really cool thing to do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25904-nika777","name":"nika777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T13:43:57-08:00","id":1469661,"title":"","content":"So,snapping your finger and making a mountain sounds nice,any other things i can do by spending a whole lot of legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T22:23:11-08:00","id":1469696,"title":"","content":"<br /> This is a question that may have been covered (haven't had a chance to go through 2e and only have Hero and Companion in 1e), but do the children of Heroes &amp; Demigods have a chance of being a Scion? Like two members of a band find themselves falling in love and end up starting a family while in their pregodhood stages, I mean the ichor is there and who knows. <br /> I ask mainly because of a bit of fan fiction I'm pondering for another property but I want to keep the mechanics right. But I really think I would actually be willing to play that type of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27210-fereality","name":"fereality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27210_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T19:46:08-08:00","id":1469795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469152#post1469152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No Fatebounding for Gods to countries/nations even?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The worshippers, cults, religions, and other peoples that Gods generally get Fatebound to exist separately of national boundaries. Like, if Odin got Fatebound to a large group of worshippers, specifying a nation would be odd, since even within a specific sect of people, you'll have members from all over The World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T19:53:20-08:00","id":1469797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nika777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469405#post1469405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you guys reveal any preliminary thoughts on how pantheon creation is going to go, for players who want to start their own faith seperate from the ones in the book? Mainly, is this going to be very freeform with guidelines on how to handle it at the table, or are there mechanics planned to attach to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries of The World has a chapter on creating your own pantheon, using the Atlantean Teros as an example. There are even design notes and guidance within the Teros that explain how you can translate existing (or entirely new) myth into designing Gods and their roles within their Pantheon.<br /> <br /> As far as mechanics that go into how cults and religions will work in God, they'll support tying those into whichever Pantheon you want, which includes custom ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T20:03:05-08:00","id":1469798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469661#post1469661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So,snapping your finger and making a mountain sounds nice,any other things i can do by spending a whole lot of legend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, while Scion: God's going to specifically name some cool things, the only real limits to what you can do by spending Legend are:<ul><li>How much Legend you have to spend</li> <li>Your imagination</li> <li>How much someone else will care and be able to resist your effect</li> </ul><br /> After all, if you stroll into Heaven and decide to rearrange a big chunk of it into a shopping mall, it's probably not going to last long. Even if you dump 12 Legend into it, there are so many Shen that a group of them will probably revert everything you did. But, if you wanted to make your own Midrealm, you could probably get away with that without problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T20:12:23-08:00","id":1469800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fereality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469696#post1469696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question that may have been covered (haven't had a chance to go through 2e and only have Hero and Companion in 1e), but do the children of Heroes &amp; Demigods have a chance of being a Scion? Like two members of a band find themselves falling in love and end up starting a family while in their pregodhood stages, I mean the ichor is there and who knows.<br /> I ask mainly because of a bit of fan fiction I'm pondering for another property but I want to keep the mechanics right. But I really think I would actually be willing to play that type of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sure. Technically, someone doesn't even need to be related to a God to become a Scion. Chosen of Gods are one of the main types of Scions.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Scion of a Hero-tier character is pretty unlikely, simply because they're not terribly powerful, but the child of a Scion could 100% be a Scion of the same God. The line gets pretty blurry at Demigod tier. Like Heracles/Hercules is generally considered a Demigod, but a ton of his children would probably be considered Scions. <br /> <br /> ALSO! Someone could retroactively become a Scion once their divine parent became powerful enough. Like, two Hero-tier Scions could have a child, who seems normal enough at birth, but gradually becomes more powerful as divine parents do, until they're powerful enough to take charge of their own destiny, eventually overshadowing their parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T08:08:18-08:00","id":1469836,"title":"","content":"are there any titans or other antagonists in God you can name drop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T23:59:51-08:00","id":1470586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469836#post1469836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are there any titans or other antagonists in God you can name drop?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at this point, but that'll change as we get closer to the finish line and the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T12:29:18-08:00","id":1470729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1469798#post1469798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, while Scion: God's going to specifically name some cool things, the only real limits to what you can do by spending Legend are:<ul><li>How much Legend you have to spend</li> <li>Your imagination</li> <li>How much someone else will care and be able to resist your effect</li> </ul><br /> <br /> After all, if you stroll into Heaven and decide to rearrange a big chunk of it into a shopping mall, it's probably not going to last long. Even if you dump 12 Legend into it, there are so many Shen that a group of them will probably revert everything you did. But, if you wanted to make your own Midrealm, you could probably get away with that without problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reads like gods will have more chances to spend big chunks of Legend. Will they have more means to replenish them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T17:32:38-08:00","id":1471410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1470729#post1470729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It reads like gods will have more chances to spend big chunks of Legend. Will they have more means to replenish them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, although exactly how much they get and from what sources is something that requires further fine-tuning, so I can't get into much detail about the mechanics except by saying that being a responsible God will replenish Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T17:43:24-08:00","id":1471411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1471410#post1471410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, although exactly how much they get and from what sources is something that requires further fine-tuning, so I can't get into much detail about the mechanics except by saying that being a responsible God will replenish Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>About Gods, I can't help but notice that different mythocosmos have different ideas of divinity. In India a God is a aspect of Infinity,in Ireland they're more like ultra fae. Does the book talks about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T20:09:00-08:00","id":1471419,"title":"","content":"I have a couple rules clarification questions, regarding a potential conflict in the Origin rulebook. I've been looking for a while, but can't find any informaiton online. If you could clarify, I would appreciate it!<br /> <br /> 1. According to my reading of the &quot;Building Legend&quot; sidebar on page 164 of Origin, it seems like Kitsune do not gain a (supernatural?) tail until they gain a point of Legend. Am I correct in assuming that this means that Origin-level Kitsune, without a Legend score, do not have to worry about hiding a tail in human form?<br /> <br /> 2. If my reading of the sidebar is correct, could you clarify the function of the &quot;Mortal Mask&quot; knack? If I'm understanding the description correctly, it serves two functions: 1) to hide a Kitsune's tail while in human form (which, again, Origin-level kitsune don't have), and 2) to keep them from being automatically identified by another being with a Legend score. Is that right? (I apologize, that just seems a little... underwhelming to me.)<br /> <br /> Thanks so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27195-brokenimage321","user":"brokenimage321","date":". 12-28-2021, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27195-brokenimage321","name":"brokenimage321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T13:02:44-08:00","id":1472017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1471411#post1471411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Gods, I can't help but notice that different mythocosmos have different ideas of divinity. In India a God is a aspect of Infinity,in Ireland they're more like ultra fae. Does the book talks about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different cultures' concepts of divinity is a difficult topic to tackle in general, but especially in Scion. God will touch on that a bit, but a well-formed answer is going to beyond the scope of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T13:03:43-08:00","id":1472019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brokenimage321</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1471419#post1471419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a couple rules clarification questions, regarding a potential conflict in the Origin rulebook. I've been looking for a while, but can't find any informaiton online. If you could clarify, I would appreciate it!<br /> <br /> 1. According to my reading of the &quot;Building Legend&quot; sidebar on page 164 of Origin, it seems like Kitsune do not gain a (supernatural?) tail until they gain a point of Legend. Am I correct in assuming that this means that Origin-level Kitsune, without a Legend score, do not have to worry about hiding a tail in human form?<br /> <br /> 2. If my reading of the sidebar is correct, could you clarify the function of the &quot;Mortal Mask&quot; knack? If I'm understanding the description correctly, it serves two functions: 1) to hide a Kitsune's tail while in human form (which, again, Origin-level kitsune don't have), and 2) to keep them from being automatically identified by another being with a Legend score. Is that right? (I apologize, that just seems a little... underwhelming to me.)<br /> <br /> Thanks so much!</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Mortal Mask probably should have been a Hero-tier Knack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T04:22:34-08:00","id":1473744,"title":"","content":"What are y'all most proud of in the Scion line? A mechanic you thought clicked, a bit of flavor text or GM advice you think really shined, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25904-nika777","name":"nika777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T15:04:11-08:00","id":1474330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nika777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1473744#post1473744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are y'all most proud of in the Scion line? A mechanic you thought clicked, a bit of flavor text or GM advice you think really shined, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's a good question. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm probably most proud of the team. Team Scion continually surprises me with the depth of their knowledge, research ability, and creativity. It's a hard act to balance paying respect to modern cultures, paying respect to Gods, and making sure that the gameplay experiences are still fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T11:27:03-07:00","id":1476330,"title":"","content":"The Contacts entry on page 100 of Scion: Origin states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">A character gains two points per invocation to use to</span> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">create her Contacts. She can spend these dots on either</span> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">gaining additional Contacts, or making a single Contact</span> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">better. Each Contact begins with one dot and one tag (see</span> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">list of suggested tags below; feel free to add your own spe</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">cial traits depending on your needs). Each additional point</span> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">placed in a single Contact adds either an additional dot or</span> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">an additional tag,</span> </div> </div> </div>If I understand this correctly, every time I want to &quot;invoke&quot; a Contact, I get two dots to spend to either boost that Contact or create additional Contacts.<br /> <br /> So I could have one Contact that starts at one dot and with one tag, and spend the two points to give them a combination of more dots and/or more tags, or I can use one of the dots to gain a second Contact and the other to add a dot or tag to either of them, or I can use both tags to gain extra Contacts, leaving me with three one dot Contacts.<br /> <br /> If this is correct, there are some questions this leaves me with:<br /> <br /> 1). What is the benefit to having multiple weaker Contacts when I can only invoke a Contact once per session?<br /> <br /> 2). If I invoke multiple Contacts, do all my Contacts have to show up at the same time?<br /> <br /> 3). Why does the character sheet has lines for Contacts if you're expected to generate new ones each time you invoke your Path?<br /> <br /> 4). Is there a way to improve your Contacts so you have more dots to spend on them? The Experience chart on page 113 implies you can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 03-13-2022, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T22:26:18-07:00","id":1476635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1476330#post1476330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Contacts entry on page 100 of Scion: Origin states:<br /> <br /> If I understand this correctly, every time I want to &quot;invoke&quot; a Contact, I get two dots to spend to either boost that Contact or create additional Contacts.<br /> <br /> So I could have one Contact that starts at one dot and with one tag, and spend the two points to give them a combination of more dots and/or more tags, or I can use one of the dots to gain a second Contact and the other to add a dot or tag to either of them, or I can use both tags to gain extra Contacts, leaving me with three one dot Contacts.<br /> <br /> If this is correct, there are some questions this leaves me with:<br /> <br /> 1). What is the benefit to having multiple weaker Contacts when I can only invoke a Contact once per session?<br /> <br /> 2). If I invoke multiple Contacts, do all my Contacts have to show up at the same time?<br /> <br /> 3). Why does the character sheet has lines for Contacts if you're expected to generate new ones each time you invoke your Path?<br /> <br /> 4). Is there a way to improve your Contacts so you have more dots to spend on them? The Experience chart on page 113 implies you can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Path Connections are a little finicky with Scion because Paths are less important to Scions than they are for characters in other Storypath games, but essentially yes, that's how it works. <br /> <br /> 1. Because you have 3 Paths, and each Path provides a Contact. You can invoke each Path once per session, meaning that you can pump up all 3 Contacts in the same session if you want. That naturally encourages you to diversify your Contacts a bit. That said, if you want more than 3 Contacts, because you're in the middle of nowhere and need someone to jump in and offer a hand, it makes more sense for that to be a &quot;new&quot; old friend from back home than it does for it to be an existing Contact who has to drive 200 miles to get to you.<br /> <br /> 2. They don't have to. In fact, they don't necessarily have to show up in person at all. They might just offer a quick pointer, piece of wisdom, or researched info by text message or something if that makes more sense. <br /> <br /> e.g. Dudeface Jones needs to break into a warehouse and FaceTimes his Contact Sneaks McGee (Thief **). Dudeface points his phone at the warehouse and Sneaks suggests raking the door's lock, giving Dudeface a 2 Enhancement to his Subterfuge roll. Once the door's open, a minotaur standing just inside glares at him and picks up a crowbar. Dudeface points his phone at the minotaur and yells for Sneaks to put Facepuncher Vasquez (Dangerous **) on the line. Facepuncher takes a look at the minotaur, notes that she's left handed and not wearing good shoes on a slick concrete floor, and tells Dudeface to duck under the crowbar and try knocking her over. Dudeface gets the 2 Enhancement to that roll and presumably floors Cathy the minotaur on her first day as a security guard.<br /> <br /> 3. You don't have to write down Contacts who are one-offs, but if you've been investing in a handful of them, you'll probably want to keep their information handy.<br /> <br /> 4. You don't need to spend Experience to improve your Contacts. By invoking each of your Paths once a session, you can have 3 Contacts, all at *****, with 2 tags each by the end of Session 3. If you pushed your luck by invoking each Path a second time each session and getting Path Suspended for each Path, each session, you could have 3 Contacts, each at *****, with 5 tags each by the end of Session 3. That's kind of a weird munchkin approach to Contacts, but you could do it if you really wanted to have a bunch of top-notch trusted Contacts. Although, if you gamed the system that hard, your SG would be justified in putting one or more of them in peril to make you work a little harder to keep your awesome Contacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T18:51:31-07:00","id":1476910,"title":"","content":"Hiiii<br /> How does creating a new pantheon inside the game story works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-01T17:11:38-07:00","id":1477876,"title":"","content":"Hi. Can you tell us what Pantheons are slated to appear in God at this point?<br /> <br /> And are there plans to include Pantheons in additional supplements beyond God? Or is there a sense that there would be diminishing returns in terms of adding something new to the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T18:26:00-07:00","id":1478532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1476910#post1476910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiiii<br /> How does creating a new pantheon inside the game story works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by that.<br /> <br /> If you mean, &quot;How do we make a new Pantheon?&quot; the mechanics and guidance on making a Pantheon (either a wholly original one or one based on a culture) are in Mysteries of the World.<br /> <br /> If you mean, &quot;How does The World react to a new Pantheon coming into existence?&quot; then the complete answer will be in God, but the gist is &quot;it depends.&quot; My preference is that The World rewrites itself so that the new Pantheon always was, although some folks may still have memories of a time before the new Pantheon existed. But, you aren't locked into my interpretation. Legend does strange things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T18:39:23-07:00","id":1478534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muskrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1477876#post1477876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Can you tell us what Pantheons are slated to appear in God at this point?<br /> <br /> And are there plans to include Pantheons in additional supplements beyond God? Or is there a sense that there would be diminishing returns in terms of adding something new to the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can tell you 3 of the 5; the last two I'm saving for the Kickstarter campaign.<br /> <br /> The Zemi of the Taino people of Puerto Rico, Hispaniola, Jamaica, Cuba, the Bahamas, and other parts of the Caribbean,<br /> the Balahala of the Visayan people of the Philippines and <br /> the Ilhm of the Canaan and Phoenician peoples.<br /> <br /> We'll probably have more Pantheon write ups in the future. There's probably something to the idea of diminishing returns, but I feel my role as the line developer carries the implicit task of advocating for people and their cultures; I'm not about to shirk that responsibility. There are plenty of cultures out there who haven't gotten their time in the sun yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T11:23:19-07:00","id":1478583,"title":"","content":"Hi there! I have a question for you:<br /> <br /> I'm working on a product for the Storypath Nexus, one which would add an American pantheon to the game (e.g., Uncle Sam, The Unknown Soldier, Florida Man, etc.). I'm trying really hard to be culturally sensitive, especially since American politics are... rather <i>fraught</i> at the moment. <br /> <br /> I recently heard that Columbia had a writeup in the first printing of the Mysteries of the World supplement, but that it was removed due to political concerns. Do you still happen to have the text for that writeup? If so, would you be willing to share it? Also, could you speak to the concerns that led to her being cut in the first place? (I'd like to be aware of what I'm getting into.)<br /> <br /> I know that this is a little more delicate subject than some of the others in this thread, so I'd be happy to continue this exchange via email or PM, if it would make things easier. <br /> <br /> Thanks!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27195-brokenimage321","name":"brokenimage321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T11:38:01-07:00","id":1478584,"title":"","content":"Not a line Dev; but my understanding is that the write-up was removed because they didn't want it to be \u201cofficial\u201d. There are a number of us who participated in the mysteries of the world kickstarter, and still have the draft copy from them; ask around, and I'm sure you'll be able to find someone willing to share the relevant text.<br /> <br /> Also, there is a republic Pantheon available in the Nexus which also includes a write-up of columbia. As it overlaps with what you're trying to do, you might want to look it over to avoid stepping on toes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T15:48:07-07:00","id":1478612,"title":"","content":"The issue with Columbia is the topic required way more text than the quick divine patron writeup in the Mysteries of the World draft to give the topic the nuance it requires. Many people felt the MotW text was too quick to just blame her association with Manifest Destiny on bad actors misusing her image, instead of exploring how she and the ideology she represents are inherently inseparable from that history.<br /> <br /> As I pointed out at the time, it\u2019s one thing to contrast (for example) Jesus with how people have misused His name to commit atrocities, when you have source texts to contrast those atrocities with, but in Columbia\u2019s case where the political propaganda IS THE SOURCE TEXT, there isn\u2019t some other Columbia you can contrast that with.<br /> <br /> (I bring up manifest destiny as the history of the usage of Columbia in that context is pretty overwhelming and bad. The record of her usage with regard to America\u2019s other original sin is a lot better, as her as Phrygian capped Liberty was generally a favored symbol of abolitionists, and hated by slavery-defenders).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-11-2022, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T07:14:02-07:00","id":1478685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1478534#post1478534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can tell you 3 of the 5; the last two I'm saving for the Kickstarter campaign.<br /> <br /> The Zemi of the Taino people of Puerto Rico, Hispaniola, Jamaica, Cuba, the Bahamas, and other parts of the Caribbean,<br /> the Balahala of the Visayan people of the Philippines and<br /> the Ilhm of the Canaan and Phoenician peoples.<br /> <br /> We'll probably have more Pantheon write ups in the future. There's probably something to the idea of diminishing returns, but I feel my role as the line developer carries the implicit task of advocating for people and their cultures; I'm not about to shirk that responsibility. There are plenty of cultures out there who haven't gotten their time in the sun yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. As a practicing Buddhist, I'm hoping we'll still get to see the Tibetan Buddhist pantheon that was being talked about at one point. And I'd love to see more Native North American pantheons, though I recognize that may be challenging given the high ethical standards Onyx Path is maintaining in representing the beliefs of living indigenous peoples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T18:32:58-07:00","id":1479566,"title":"","content":"As God is coming (man, that sounded VERY prophetic), I have a question, not exactly about how it works, but if the book deals with it.<br /> <br /> Diferent cultures have different ways they see the gods among us, and I want to know if the book deals with it or if all gods can manifest equally, independent of their myths.<br /> <br /> To my limited knowledge, the Theoi can be any form they wish, and belong to the material world, where they were born and grew, while Olympus (the realm, not the mountain) is just the place they call home, while it is kind of anchored to the top of the mountain. Their avatars are part of themselves, manifested by their will as they can be anything, including many things at same time.<br /> The Aesir works kind of the same way, they are born in Asgaard, but they are as physical as it\u2019s possible, they can do amazing things, but they are kind of locked in their physical bodies, and only can affect the place they are in (kind of\u2026 they have powers and relics to reach further) and they rely on golden apples to live forever (not naturally immortals).<br /> The Netjer are different, they don\u2019t walk in the world with their bodies, they are powerful spirits that need people (occasionally animals) to have proper physical bodies, and their natural place is their realm, where they are more solid. Their avatars are part of their powers invested into people (for example pharaohs), and they can have multiple avatars, by splitting their power among multiple subjects.<br /> <br /> Basically, Aesir are human-like aliens that use magic and their natural powers to control the elements, Netjer are Wraiths that can manifest in the world by the use of their powers/magic, but still need to control someone else body if they want to be material, and Theoi are formless magical beings with the power to do lots of random things.<br /> <br /> I may have a very limited knowledge, and my description is very simplistic, but I am almost sure the way the many cultures see their gods can be described in many different ways that don\u2019t fit the way it was described in Scion 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T10:35:32-07:00","id":1479590,"title":"","content":"So, quick question: In the Backer PDF, I noticed that Dominion Boons no longer state that they require spending 2 boon slots to obtain like it did in the manuscript. Is this a mistake, or a mechanical change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T11:18:56-07:00","id":1479593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479590#post1479590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, quick question: In the Backer PDF, I noticed that Dominion Boons no longer state that they require spending 2 boon slots to obtain like it did in the manuscript. Is this a mistake, or a mechanical change?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am almost sure it was a big mistake in the manuscript too, basically it was not properly described and we got it from the devs during the KS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-27-2022, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T16:07:45-07:00","id":1479608,"title":"","content":"So, in the picture showing the 'old mythical' version of the Annuna pantheon why are they grey and statue like? Is that just some unfinished art thats not been colored in yet or was that on purpose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T07:10:44-07:00","id":1479694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479590#post1479590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, quick question: In the Backer PDF, I noticed that Dominion Boons no longer state that they require spending 2 boon slots to obtain like it did in the manuscript. Is this a mistake, or a mechanical change?</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading the chapter again, it is amazingly unclear how do we develop dominions over purviews. It describes very well how to use it and the advantages are well explained, but it just says &quot;if you have dominion&quot; or &quot;all character that have dominion&quot; and &quot;if multiple character have dominion over the same purview&quot;.<br /> <br /> Its not clear what is to have dominion, is it when you have a dominion boon? Is it a Knack? Is it a new trait Demigods and Gods have but heroes dont?<br /> My guess is it is: If yu have a Dominion Boon of a purview, you have dominion over it, and Dominion boons cost 2 boons slots, as it was described duing the KS, but it is not in the book at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T09:35:33-07:00","id":1479705,"title":"","content":"If that's so, I think someone needs to submit some errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T11:58:56-07:00","id":1479726,"title":"","content":"What happens if a character who has Scent the Divine comes near a character who is actively trying to conceal their presence? Does it just auto-defeat stealth attempts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-29-2022, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T07:08:18-07:00","id":1479805,"title":"","content":"Hi Hiromi,<br /> <br /> I saw you said earlier that most of the Origin and Hero rules you've had to learn along with the players. I was wondering now that you're the line Dev, what your recommendation would be for handling some of the discrepancies regarding Virtues and Momentum.<br /> <br /> I know the fix for the regular Virtue and Momentum system isn't too hard to tweak and there's a few popular options discussed on the Discord, but I'm curious what your recommendation would be. Also, I'm interested in what your fixes would be to some of the periphery systems.<br /> <br /> Specifically the Innate power for Yoga, the Deva PSP. It currently reads:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once per scene, when you act selflessly despite hardships in order to uphold a duty or serve someone else, you may allow another player to spend Momentum on an action without having to draw on one of their Virtues. Every point of Momentum they spend also adds another free die, as though they had the Virtuous Condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to contain some artifact text that implies you can ONLY use Momentum when drawing on a Virtue and then grants the Scion the Virtuous condition on top of that. What would your recommended fix for this be?<br /> <br /> Similarly, I've already submitted errata for this as it's likely an error, but the Demigod backer manuscript has a section under Gaining Divinity Dice, which refers to any dice added from Virtues counting as divinity dice, including when doubled using Momentum, which also seems to be out of left field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T17:39:55-07:00","id":1480600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brokenimage321</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1478583#post1478583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there! I have a question for you:<br /> <br /> I'm working on a product for the Storypath Nexus, one which would add an American pantheon to the game (e.g., Uncle Sam, The Unknown Soldier, Florida Man, etc.). I'm trying really hard to be culturally sensitive, especially since American politics are... rather <i>fraught</i> at the moment.<br /> <br /> I recently heard that Columbia had a writeup in the first printing of the Mysteries of the World supplement, but that it was removed due to political concerns. Do you still happen to have the text for that writeup? If so, would you be willing to share it? Also, could you speak to the concerns that led to her being cut in the first place? (I'd like to be aware of what I'm getting into.)<br /> <br /> I know that this is a little more delicate subject than some of the others in this thread, so I'd be happy to continue this exchange via email or PM, if it would make things easier.<br /> <br /> Thanks!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow. It's been a minute since I've checked this thread.<br /> <br /> That was before I took over, but yeah, your fellow posters have the gist of it. There's not really a good way to do an American Pantheon (or any other nationalist Pantheon, for that matter). Tying Gods and nationalism together is a particularly thorny bush, so we're just going to not. Folks are still free to update the 1e material and/or make their own version for the Storypath Nexus, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T17:42:07-07:00","id":1480601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muskrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1478685#post1478685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. As a practicing Buddhist, I'm hoping we'll still get to see the Tibetan Buddhist pantheon that was being talked about at one point. And I'd love to see more Native North American pantheons, though I recognize that may be challenging given the high ethical standards Onyx Path is maintaining in representing the beliefs of living indigenous peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to see the Palas, as well as Indigenous cultures represented in Scion. Stay tuned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T17:52:51-07:00","id":1480603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479566#post1479566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As God is coming (man, that sounded VERY prophetic), I have a question, not exactly about how it works, but if the book deals with it.<br /> <br /> Diferent cultures have different ways they see the gods among us, and I want to know if the book deals with it or if all gods can manifest equally, independent of their myths.<br /> <br /> To my limited knowledge, the Theoi can be any form they wish, and belong to the material world, where they were born and grew, while Olympus (the realm, not the mountain) is just the place they call home, while it is kind of anchored to the top of the mountain. Their avatars are part of themselves, manifested by their will as they can be anything, including many things at same time.<br /> The Aesir works kind of the same way, they are born in Asgaard, but they are as physical as it\u2019s possible, they can do amazing things, but they are kind of locked in their physical bodies, and only can affect the place they are in (kind of\u2026 they have powers and relics to reach further) and they rely on golden apples to live forever (not naturally immortals).<br /> The Netjer are different, they don\u2019t walk in the world with their bodies, they are powerful spirits that need people (occasionally animals) to have proper physical bodies, and their natural place is their realm, where they are more solid. Their avatars are part of their powers invested into people (for example pharaohs), and they can have multiple avatars, by splitting their power among multiple subjects.<br /> <br /> Basically, Aesir are human-like aliens that use magic and their natural powers to control the elements, Netjer are Wraiths that can manifest in the world by the use of their powers/magic, but still need to control someone else body if they want to be material, and Theoi are formless magical beings with the power to do lots of random things.<br /> <br /> I may have a very limited knowledge, and my description is very simplistic, but I am almost sure the way the many cultures see their gods can be described in many different ways that don\u2019t fit the way it was described in Scion 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pantheon-specific limitations on manifesting in The World or other realms is not something that's terribly feasible from a mechanical standpoint. Like, it's an interesting idea that would help better ground the various Gods in their cultural stories, but that'll create inherent inequality among the Pantheons. It would also require that reaching a consensus on what the myths have to say about how a Pantheon manifests among mortals, which would be a tall order, given just how many myths and versions of those myths exist.<br /> <br /> So, to answer your question, all of the Gods are on the same footing in The World, although getting to and from The World might pose special challenges based on where their home is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T18:02:40-07:00","id":1480608,"title":"","content":"Can you tell us more about how a a brand new pantheon is created inside the story of the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T18:43:53-07:00","id":1480611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479590#post1479590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, quick question: In the Backer PDF, I noticed that Dominion Boons no longer state that they require spending 2 boon slots to obtain like it did in the manuscript. Is this a mistake, or a mechanical change?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't directly answer that. While I've taken over steering the line, Neall's still in charge of Demigod. Once the dust settles on Demigod, I'll clarify any further questions folks have. I know this isn't immediately helpful for you or the other folks who've expressed confusion about Dominion, but the best that I can do without creating further confusion.<br /> <br /> In the meantime! If anything about Dominion Boons and their stunts is confusing or seems off, please use the errata form to help get it addressed: <a href=\"https://forms.gle/5rWPu8mFWdU1a1uN6\" target=\"_blank\">errata link</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T19:03:55-07:00","id":1480613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479608#post1479608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the picture showing the 'old mythical' version of the Annuna pantheon why are they grey and statue like? Is that just some unfinished art thats not been colored in yet or was that on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm believe that was an intentional choice, reflecting their connection to clay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T19:36:59-07:00","id":1480618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479726#post1479726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a character who has Scent the Divine comes near a character who is actively trying to conceal their presence? Does it just auto-defeat stealth attempts?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 important caveats with Scent the Divine:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Scent the Divine specifically says that it &quot;detects&quot; when such a being is nearby. &quot;Detect&quot; is not a keyword, so there's some wiggle room on what exactly that means.</li> <li>Anytime two supernatural abilities interfere with each other, it triggers a Clash of Wills (Origin, p. 105)</li> </ol>So, no. Stealth isn't automatically defeated, but if the Scion with Scent the Divine active wins the Clash of Wills, they have at least a rough idea of where the divine being is.<br /> <br /> As a personal rule of thumb, I'd say they know what range band the divine being is in and the general direction, gaining an Enhancement to any rolls to pinpoint that being. But, that's my interpretation of &quot;detect,&quot; not an official one, at least not yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":27136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","user":"Hiromi","date":".  Cut out one of the limitations because it's not good game design. 05-19-2022, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T20:11:19-07:00","id":1480624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>demonchilde</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1479805#post1479805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Hiromi,<br /> <br /> I saw you said earlier that most of the Origin and Hero rules you've had to learn along with the players. I was wondering now that you're the line Dev, what your recommendation would be for handling some of the discrepancies regarding Virtues and Momentum.<br /> <br /> I know the fix for the regular Virtue and Momentum system isn't too hard to tweak and there's a few popular options discussed on the Discord, but I'm curious what your recommendation would be. Also, I'm interested in what your fixes would be to some of the periphery systems.<br /> <br /> Specifically the Innate power for Yoga, the Deva PSP. It currently reads:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once per scene, when you act selflessly despite hardships in order to uphold a duty or serve someone else, you may allow another player to spend Momentum on an action without having to draw on one of their Virtues. Every point of Momentum they spend also adds another free die, as though they had the Virtuous Condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to contain some artifact text that implies you can ONLY use Momentum when drawing on a Virtue and then grants the Scion the Virtuous condition on top of that. What would your recommended fix for this be?<br /> <br /> Similarly, I've already submitted errata for this as it's likely an error, but the Demigod backer manuscript has a section under Gaining Divinity Dice, which refers to any dice added from Virtues counting as divinity dice, including when doubled using Momentum, which also seems to be out of left field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's some odd wording. I suspect that wording reflects an earlier version of Momentum and an earlier version of Virtue that both no longer exist.<br /> <br /> I think the easiest tweak to Yoga's wording to bring it in line with the rest of the rules would be that instead of &quot;without having to draw on...&quot; if it said &quot;as if they had augmented their roll with ...&quot; <br /> <br /> That way, you spend your innate for the scene, then your ally gets gets to add an additional die per point of Virtue per Momentum they're adding. Then, if they're not already at +2 (and thus already have the Virtuous Condition), they get another +1 per Momentum.<ul><li>Example 1: You use Yoga. Little Mao's at 0 Yin/Yang. Mendez spends 2 Momentum on a Close Combat + Dexterity roll that has nothing to do with Yin or Yang.<ul><li>+2 dice (Momentum) +0 (Yin 0 *2d) +2d (Virtuous) = +4d for 2 Momentum.</li> </ul></li> <li>Example 2: Little Mao's at 1 Yin. Mendez spends 3 Momentum on a roll that doesn't have anything to do with Yin.<ul><li>+3d (Momentum) +3d (Yin 1*3d) + 3 (Virtuous) = +9d for 3 Momentum</li> </ul></li> <li>Example 3: Little Mao's at 2 Yin. Mendez spends everything in the pool \u2014 6 Momentum \u2014 on a Persuasion + Presence to rock the mic, even though that's not very Yin.<ul><li>+6d (Momentum) +12d (Yin 2*6d) + 6 (Virtuous) = + 24d for 6 Momentum.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> So, my tweak would make it clear that you don't need to act in accordance with your Virtue in order to spend Momentum, but there's kind of an underlying problem that being Virtuous is <b>really</b> good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T20:18:05-07:00","id":1480626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1480608#post1480608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you tell us more about how a a brand new pantheon is created inside the story of the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't let on more than I did the last you asked, but I'll definitely be talking about that once we get closer to God's Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T01:11:54-07:00","id":1480641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1480603#post1480603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pantheon-specific limitations on manifesting in The World or other realms is not something that's terribly feasible from a mechanical standpoint. Like, it's an interesting idea that would help better ground the various Gods in their cultural stories, but that'll create inherent inequality among the Pantheons. It would also require that reaching a consensus on what the myths have to say about how a Pantheon manifests among mortals, which would be a tall order, given just how many myths and versions of those myths exist.<br /> <br /> So, to answer your question, all of the Gods are on the same footing in The World, although getting to and from The World might pose special challenges based on where their home is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! That's a very solid way to say no, while at same time giving a hint on how to deal with it. The ins and outs of their godrelms and the nature of their PSP would give some explanation on why they manifest the way they do in their myths, if not their own choices as a pantheon. Thanks again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T03:42:18-07:00","id":1480650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1480626#post1480626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't let on more than I did the last you asked, but I'll definitely be talking about that once we get closer to God's Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I forgot I already asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T19:44:31-07:00","id":1481508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1480618#post1480618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 important caveats with Scent the Divine:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Scion has to declare the Pantheon to be detected. Divine beings not connected to that Pantheon aren't picked up.</li> <li>Scent the Divine specifically says that it &quot;detects&quot; when such a being is nearby. &quot;Detect&quot; is not a keyword, so there's some wiggle room on what exactly that means.</li> <li>Anytime two supernatural abilities interfere with each other, it triggers a Clash of Wills (Origin, p. 105)</li> </ol>So, no. Stealth isn't automatically defeated, but if the Scion with Scent the Divine active wins the Clash of Wills, they have at least a rough idea of where the divine being is.<br /> <br /> As a personal rule of thumb, I'd say they know what range band the divine being is in and the general direction, gaining an Enhancement to any rolls to pinpoint that being. But, that's my interpretation of &quot;detect,&quot; not an official one, at least not yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>On second thought, while needing to declare a target Pantheon is a valid reading of the Knack's text, it's not a particularly <i>good</i> or useful one. The other two limitations provide more than enough flexibility to make being on each side of Scent of the Divine fun.<br /> <br /> I'll edit that post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T11:28:26-07:00","id":1482014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1481508#post1481508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On second thought, while needing to declare a target Pantheon is a valid reading of the Knack's text, it's not a particularly <i>good</i> or useful one. The other two limitations provide more than enough flexibility to make being on each side of Scent of the Divine fun.<br /> <br /> I'll edit that post.</div> </div> </div> </div>About Scent the divine, on Dragon manuscript their have a \u201cupdated\u201d Scent the Divine, on book it dont seems to be a \u201cknack\u201d , it seems like a natural skill for Heirs.<br /> <br /> Its okay for Heroes use that \u201cupdated\u201d version of Scent the divine? I asking because Dragon gives unique mechanics to blow covers ( knacks transformation and etc), so considering all Dragon lore it seens a little anti-climatic a Scion be able to snuff out a Heir with just a knack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T16:43:48-07:00","id":1483259,"title":"","content":"i'm wondering these days, how the character rating on skills and dots will influence things when we playing gods in their full form like a Incarnation will be like a god and demigo character but how would a god in all his might with cunning 4 compare to a god on all his might with cunning 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T13:53:46-07:00","id":1483810,"title":"","content":"Can you tell us more about the new stuff in Wild Hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T23:07:16-07:00","id":1485171,"title":"","content":"Hello !<br /> <br /> Not used to ask something in there, but since the release of Demigod (wich was amazing, thank you for the great work !), i was wondering something : i have currently two tables of Scion on pause, one that can resume with Scions from the Japanese pantheon that can now become demigods, but another made entirely of Scions from the Irish Titans, the Tuatha de Domu. I currently know that there will be some kind of rework for the passive boons of Titan's Scion in &quot;Saints and Monster&quot;, but i don't know if it will include, in this same book, more Immortal knacks for the Titans knacks as in Demigod, or if there will be specific rules for elevating a Scion of the Titan to a &quot;Demigod&quot; status. So, basically, my question is : will the knacks and rules for Titan's Scion be expanded, and if yes, in which book ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:35:46-07:00","id":1486656,"title":"","content":"Are there any further plans for upgrades for Denizens that arenKt Scions at Demigod tier? That was a thing that Hero implied, with Kitsune going up to Demigod tier, and Valkyries being around as Demigod tier denizens, etc - but Saints and Monsters doesn\u2019t have any power upgrades for Denizens past Legend 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:15:56-07:00","id":1487125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1482014#post1482014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About Scent the divine, on Dragon manuscript their have a \u201cupdated\u201d Scent the Divine, on book it dont seems to be a \u201cknack\u201d , it seems like a natural skill for Heirs.<br /> <br /> Its okay for Heroes use that \u201cupdated\u201d version of Scent the divine? I asking because Dragon gives unique mechanics to blow covers ( knacks transformation and etc), so considering all Dragon lore it seens a little anti-climatic a Scion be able to snuff out a Heir with just a knack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as written, Scions don't get an upgrade to their version of Scent the Divine. That said, if you want to do it in your game, it's not going to cause massive headaches.<br /> <br /> Your concern that Scions might be able to sniff out a Dragon is reasonable but remember that the vast majority of Scions don't even know that Dragons are a separate faction; they either won't recognize the scent or will confuse it with some other Pantheon's scent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:27:34-07:00","id":1487127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1483259#post1483259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm wondering these days, how the character rating on skills and dots will influence things when we playing gods in their full form like a Incarnation will be like a god and demigo character but how would a god in all his might with cunning 4 compare to a god on all his might with cunning 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that it's going to come up much; it's hard to imagine a God willingly engaging in a conflict where they don't have a full 10-die pool. And, if another God is attacking their weak points, they're probably already in trouble beyond being short a dot or two.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1483810#post1483810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you tell us more about the new stuff in Wild Hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:34:49-07:00","id":1487129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Darcia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1485171#post1485171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello !<br /> <br /> Not used to ask something in there, but since the release of Demigod (wich was amazing, thank you for the great work !), i was wondering something : i have currently two tables of Scion on pause, one that can resume with Scions from the Japanese pantheon that can now become demigods, but another made entirely of Scions from the Irish Titans, the Tuatha de Domu. I currently know that there will be some kind of rework for the passive boons of Titan's Scion in &quot;Saints and Monster&quot;, but i don't know if it will include, in this same book, more Immortal knacks for the Titans knacks as in Demigod, or if there will be specific rules for elevating a Scion of the Titan to a &quot;Demigod&quot; status. So, basically, my question is : will the knacks and rules for Titan's Scion be expanded, and if yes, in which book ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you haven't already picked up Saints &amp; Monsters, it has a fair number of Immortal and Heroic Knacks specifically for Scions, so that ought to help you out there. It also includes guidance on Titanic Demigods, which can undergo Apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T02:03:23-07:00","id":1487134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1486656#post1486656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any further plans for upgrades for Denizens that arenKt Scions at Demigod tier? That was a thing that Hero implied, with Kitsune going up to Demigod tier, and Valkyries being around as Demigod tier denizens, etc - but Saints and Monsters doesn\u2019t have any power upgrades for Denizens past Legend 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T14:34:20-07:00","id":1487252,"title":"","content":"thanks hiromi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:14:54-07:00","id":1487600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1487129#post1487129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you haven't already picked up Saints &amp; Monsters, it has a fair number of Immortal and Heroic Knacks specifically for Scions, so that ought to help you out there. It also includes guidance on Titanic Demigods, which can undergo Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you very much, i have indeed bought it, and it was everything i was looking for ! Keep up the good work !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T21:52:06-07:00","id":1487688,"title":"","content":"If a Dragon takes up Sorcery, how does that work? Are they treated more like a Saint or a Scion? Inheritance isn't Legend, (notably it doesn't cause Fatebinding), and frankly Sorcery is all about using Legend to reshaping the world, not dissimilar to Fatebinding. Plus the play style of careful strategy and preparation of Sorcery fits right in there with the heist-like espionage nature of Dragon stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:25:23-07:00","id":1487694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1487688#post1487688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Dragon takes up Sorcery, how does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery Flair directly states that Dragons use Dragons Magic in this place - i.e. Dragons version of their Purviews magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion Dragon KS Manuscript p. 266</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sorcery</b><br /> (...)<br /> Choose a Dragon Magic (p. XX). The Antagonist may use Spells from that Dragon <br /> Magic for the cost of 1 Tension.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T01:25:16-07:00","id":1487701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1487694#post1487694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorcery Flair directly states that Dragons use Dragons Magic in this place - i.e. Dragons version of their Purviews magic.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, should have clairified; How do Dragons (Heirs, Lesser Wyrns, etc) interact/use with the Sorcery system from Saints and Monsters?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T02:43:40-07:00","id":1489459,"title":"","content":"In Saints and Monsters there are variations on when characters get specialties to their skills. For example Saints and Prophets get them at skill level 3 and up and they also get them if the skill is raised with the dots from final touches while Denizen characters creation gives specialties to skills above 3, so at three is not enough, and specifically says that the dots added on final touches do not grant specialties even if they raise the score to 4 of above.<br /> <br /> Are these differences intentional or a mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T01:10:31-07:00","id":1491564,"title":"","content":"So, in the Dragon book there is a side bar before the calling knacks saying that if you see a knack whose mechanics are better then the scion version you could basically consider it errata and apply the improved knack to a scion. Does the same apply to dragon magic spells vs purview powered boons? Like, for example, at hero level an Earth purview hero scion gets the boon 'shaping hand' that lets them turn rocks/metal they are directly touching malleable as clay. Meanwhile at 'hero' level an earth magic using dragon gets 'command the solid earth', which is basically full on long distance manipulation of earth/metal bending style from Avatar the Last Airbender and is clearly just vastly superior to what a hero level scion gets out of their earth manipulation boon. Honestly, its write up sounds more impressive in its examples of what can be done then anything I see <b>demigod </b>Earth scions have in terms of dominion boons (where it seems to top out at 'you raise up a single defensive earth wall' compared to heirs being told about how they can make entire buildings or dig out a new cave system).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-28-2022, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T21:22:51-07:00","id":1491869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1491564#post1491564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the Dragon book there is a side bar before the calling knacks saying that if you see a knack whose mechanics are better then the scion version you could basically consider it errata and apply the improved knack to a scion. Does the same apply to dragon magic spells vs purview powered boons? Like, for example, at hero level an Earth purview hero scion gets the boon 'shaping hand' that lets them turn rocks/metal they are directly touching malleable as clay. Meanwhile at 'hero' level an earth magic using dragon gets 'command the solid earth', which is basically full on long distance manipulation of earth/metal bending style from Avatar the Last Airbender and is clearly just vastly superior to what a hero level scion gets out of their earth manipulation boon. Honestly, its write up sounds more impressive in its examples of what can be done then anything I see <b>demigod </b>Earth scions have in terms of dominion boons (where it seems to top out at 'you raise up a single defensive earth wall' compared to heirs being told about how they can make entire buildings or dig out a new cave system).</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells are generally more broadly applicable than Boons, but Dragons don\u2019t have Marvels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T23:44:08-07:00","id":1491872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1491869#post1491869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells are generally more broadly applicable than Boons, but Dragons don\u2019t have Marvels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I mentioned, the description demigod level earth gets is less impressive then this first tier spell. While dragons are knocking over buildings or making them with their powers when in the hero league a Demigod level miracle lets a scion move 'a single large boulder' and one of their boons called 'raise the Earthen barrier' lets them raise up just enough earth to gain access to the cover mechanic. The difference between what an earth dragon and an earth scion get access to in terms of using earth to reshape the environment is staggering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T10:51:50-07:00","id":1491922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1491872#post1491872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I mentioned, the description demigod level earth gets is less impressive then this first tier spell. While dragons are knocking over buildings or making them with their powers when in the hero league a Demigod level miracle lets a scion move 'a single large boulder' and one of their boons called 'raise the Earthen barrier' lets them raise up just , nough earth to gain access to the cover mechanic. The difference between what an earth dragon and an earth scion get access to in terms of using earth to reshape the environment is staggering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have not yet accessed to Scion : Dragon, but as someone who just spent the last month compulsing all the Purviews to create a helpful guide for my table, i think the problem here is mechanical, rather than a question of &quot;are Dragon's heir more powerful than Demigods ?&quot;. Just like <b>glamourweaver</b> said, a Demigod can do what this &quot;spell&quot; is describing by using a Marvel like &quot;Attacking&quot; or &quot;Upheaval&quot;. The example you gave, the Casual Miracle, is indeed less impressive, but remember that it's completely free : no Momentum or Legend cost at all. While the Dominion Boon, still not as impressive as the spell, has the particularity that it can be granted to others, including people who don't use the Earth Purview, since Domingon makes a Demigod a nexus of power to aid their allies. <br /> <br /> Again, i don't have Dragon, but reading from your example, it strikes me more as a question of balanced mechanics : Dragon seems to have less flexibility, but more powerful spells, while a Scion has more tools, but demands that the player has more imaginations when it comes to Marvels","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T21:08:04-07:00","id":1492735,"title":"","content":"Any chance you could reveal why Lilith ended up getting removed as an example patron write up from the final product after being in the kickstarter draft of the Mythos book? And are other references to her that are still in the book supposed to be there or should we report any mention of her as an error?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 09-10-2022, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T23:45:35-07:00","id":1493458,"title":"","content":"What happens if a dragon tries to learn sorcery? And what happens if a dragon tries to gain the awareness stat after they spend some time tangling with Lovecraftian horrors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T07:26:22-07:00","id":1494039,"title":"","content":"Hi there! I hope this isn't, like, a conflict of interest or anything...<br /> <br /> I submitted a pitch for a Scion 2e supplement a few months ago, which was rejected. I've been working on it off-and-on ever since, and it has drastically changed in scope since the initial pitch, to the point where I'm considering re-submitting it.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to talk to you, or maybe someone else on the team, to get some more information about why my pitch was rejected the first time around? I'm wondering whether, say, there was no interest in the concept in the first place, whether I needed to tweak my approach, if it just wasn't the time, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27195-brokenimage321","name":"brokenimage321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T15:08:46-07:00","id":1494470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1487701#post1487701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, should have clairified; How do Dragons (Heirs, Lesser Wyrns, etc) interact/use with the Sorcery system from Saints and Monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not really an explicit way to bridge that gap. You can use the &quot;Denizens, Saints, and Sorcery&quot; sidebar on p. 77 as a template to keep a foot in each world, but that effectively treats the characters as a Sorcerer that coincidentally happens to be an Heir, as opposed to a fully hybridized character.<br /> <br /> It gets a lot easier to play in both worlds as a Full Dragon, but Dragons don't really need to mess with the Sorcery system at all since they can use any Spell they want without cost and without spending time or resources to learn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T15:55:27-07:00","id":1494472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1489459#post1489459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Saints and Monsters there are variations on when characters get specialties to their skills. For example Saints and Prophets get them at skill level 3 and up and they also get them if the skill is raised with the dots from final touches while Denizen characters creation gives specialties to skills above 3, so at three is not enough, and specifically says that the dots added on final touches do not grant specialties even if they raise the score to 4 of above.<br /> <br /> Are these differences intentional or a mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference was intentional, but I wasn't involved.<br /> <br /> Whether or not increasing a Skill to 3+ during Finishing Touches grants Specialties is a largely undefined grey area. I think most SGs (including me) assumed that the answer was &quot;yes,&quot; but there wasn't an official ruling. The Denizen character creation rules say &quot;no,&quot; but I'm not planning on carrying that answer forward. I don't have a problem with someone who really wants to focus on maximizing their Specialties, especially since they're cutting themself off from having 5* Skills to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T16:51:54-07:00","id":1494477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1491564#post1491564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the Dragon book there is a side bar before the calling knacks saying that if you see a knack whose mechanics are better then the scion version you could basically consider it errata and apply the improved knack to a scion. Does the same apply to dragon magic spells vs purview powered boons? Like, for example, at hero level an Earth purview hero scion gets the boon 'shaping hand' that lets them turn rocks/metal they are directly touching malleable as clay. Meanwhile at 'hero' level an earth magic using dragon gets 'command the solid earth', which is basically full on long distance manipulation of earth/metal bending style from Avatar the Last Airbender and is clearly just vastly superior to what a hero level scion gets out of their earth manipulation boon. Honestly, its write up sounds more impressive in its examples of what can be done then anything I see <b>demigod </b>Earth scions have in terms of dominion boons (where it seems to top out at 'you raise up a single defensive earth wall' compared to heirs being told about how they can make entire buildings or dig out a new cave system).</div> </div> </div> </div>tl;dr Rules as written, it's just Knacks, but SGs can do what they want.<br /> <br /> You are correct that Dragon Spells are in many cases more powerful than their Boon equivalents. The system wasn't really designed for mechanical balance with the rest of Scion, as it's a fairly different game in many ways. Dragon games generally focus on being stealthy; knocking down buildings will probably attract a lot of unwanted attention, possibly from dragonslayers, Gods, Scions, or even the Heir's own Flight.<br /> <br /> Dragon Companion will introduce the Heat mechanic, which codifies exactly how bad it is to be reckless in Dragon games. <br /> <br /> That said, SGs running games with both Heirs and Scions may want to get the characters a little closer in power level. If so, granting Scions access to Spells would be one way to handle that.<br /> I wouldn't recommend doing it in an all-Scion game, but if an SG really wants to, it's not like I can stop them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T16:59:20-07:00","id":1494478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1492735#post1492735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance you could reveal why Lilith ended up getting removed as an example patron write up from the final product after being in the kickstarter draft of the Mythos book? And are other references to her that are still in the book supposed to be there or should we report any mention of her as an error?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's at least 4 reasons, but the biggest is that lumping someone from Jewish folklore in with Cthulhu was insensitive, and several of us moved to cut it when we noticed.<br /> <br /> The 3 leftover mentions of her ought to be gone in the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T17:14:17-07:00","id":1494479,"title":"","content":"Hi again,Hiromi. I have a bunch of questions,but i'll limit myself to 2.<br /> are there new sorcery traditions coming?<br /> will Scion: God have a brand new sample character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T17:44:51-07:00","id":1494481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1493458#post1493458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a dragon tries to learn sorcery? And what happens if a dragon tries to gain the awareness stat after they spend some time tangling with Lovecraftian horrors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons and Sorcery don't really mix well. You can use the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Denizens, Saints, and Sorcery&quot; sidebar on p. 77 of Saints &amp; Monsters to make it kind of work, though. After Inheritance 10, Dragons can just do whatever Sorcery Spells they want and pretend like they were Sorcerers the whole time.<br /> <br /> There's not a book answer for what happens to Heirs who seek Awareness, but I don't see a reason why you couldn't cross those streams. Heirs with Awareness would be in a tight spot where they're trying to lie low at the same time that they're trying to get the Great Old Ones' attention. Such a game would probably involve a lot of secret moves and plots within plots. So, it'd be a weird game, but Mythos games are automatically weird, so it's not too farfetched.<br /> <br /> By the book, mixing Awareness &amp; Inheritance wouldn't work well unless all the players were Mythos Heirs; Heirs can't get more than 1 Inheritance ahead of their broodmates (Dragon, p.118).<br /> <br /> e.g. If a Mythos Heir completes a Deed set and raises their Awareness while the rest of the Brood increases their Inheritance, the rest of the Brood is locked out of picking new Deeds until the Mythos Heir completes another Deed set and chooses to increase their Inheritance.<br /> <br /> If you ignored that rule, then the Mythos Heir would end up lagging behind as they split their Deeds between the two resources, the same way as the only Mythos Scion in an all-Scion game would. <br /> <br /> If you ran an all Mythos Heir game, those problems would fall away, though. It'd still be weird, but as long as that doesn't get in the way of everyone's fun, I don't see a problem.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T17:47:07-07:00","id":1494482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brokenimage321</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1494039#post1494039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there! I hope this isn't, like, a conflict of interest or anything...<br /> <br /> I submitted a pitch for a Scion 2e supplement a few months ago, which was rejected. I've been working on it off-and-on ever since, and it has drastically changed in scope since the initial pitch, to the point where I'm considering re-submitting it.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to talk to you, or maybe someone else on the team, to get some more information about why my pitch was rejected the first time around? I'm wondering whether, say, there was no interest in the concept in the first place, whether I needed to tweak my approach, if it just wasn't the time, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about an actual pitch or a writing submission? <br /> <br /> Writing submissions are effectively auditions, letting us see what you can do so that you can get hired for a book later down the line.<br /> <br /> If you sent a pitch it, I didn't receive it, but I also don't get sent pitches directly. So, it got bounced somewhere above me. Number one reason submissions get bounced is for not following all of the instructions, including the disclosure form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T17:56:13-07:00","id":1494483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1494479#post1494479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi again,Hiromi. I have a bunch of questions,but i'll limit myself to 2.<br /> are there new sorcery traditions coming?<br /> will Scion: God have a brand new sample character?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan on getting Sorcerers some love in the future, but won't be able to elaborate on that for awhile. You shouldn't expect a significant Sorcerer expansion in the near future.<br /> <br /> As to your second question, yes, but no. That answer will make more sense in a few weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T14:04:11-07:00","id":1495189,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm jumping the gun here, but ... one of the things I like most about Scion is the pantheon write-ups. Do you foresee more pantheons coming out after God (which I have already backed)? In what context would they come out? Do you see a big book of pantheons as something that might be done? Or would they appear in the context of supplements on other topics--I've seen some talk of the Welsh gods being featured in the Arthurian supplement. (If you go that route, it might also be interesting to include the Scythian gods, given the existence of the Sarmatian hypothesis--that the legends of King Arthur were inspired by Sarmatian (Scythian) cavalry serving the Roman Empire in Britain and that elements of the Arthurian mythos are deriving from Sarmatian mythology.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T09:42:52-07:00","id":1495317,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to get a few examples of what the Mythos Order Boon, Lawful Trespass, is meant to do in the context of ignoring a &quot;Law of Physics?&quot;<br /> <br /> The more examples the better, honestly. This one is hard for me to wrap my head around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T00:05:26-07:00","id":1495345,"title":"","content":"Hello :<br /> <br /> My question is maybe a bit out of topic, but i don't know where else to post it. I am french and a big fan of Scion since my friends introduced me to the first edition, translated by a french company now defunct. Reading the second edition is a real pleasure, as i am comfortable enough in english, but introducing the game to some of my friends has been sometimes complicated, since i had to write up guides in french so they could clearly understand the rules (not all of them read english). So, my question is basically twofold : do you plan on translating Scion 2e to other language, and if so, how would it work ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T22:18:27-07:00","id":1495799,"title":"","content":"So, in regards to Titan Scions in Saints and Monsters, the character creation segment under Finishing Touches says that the Titanic Scions should pick their Virtue based on their associated patheon. At first I thought this might be a typo and there was an &quot;s&quot; missing, but the example creation of the Scion of Jord, then has the player only select Audacity as their Virtue and neglects Fatalism.<br /> <br /> So what was the intent behind this? Is there a special system for Titan Scions and Virtues that didn't make it into the final book? Or something that is in the book and I keep overlooking it? What happens if they hit the end of the Virtue track and become Virtuous, what brings them back into balance without another Virtue to act upon?<br /> <br /> Or am I reading too much into it and it's just a typo that then got picked up and carried into the example portion of creation as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","user":"demonchilde","date":". 10-29-2022, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T20:33:32-08:00","id":1496956,"title":"","content":"What flights are the Tarasque and the Ismenian Dragon in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27668-mrred","name":"MrRed","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T21:54:27-08:00","id":1498738,"title":"","content":"Am I correct that Legendary Denizens can use their Denizen Keywords to gain +1 Scale, but lack the Titles necessary to ever perform a Feat of Scale to gain 1/2 Legend (round up) Scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:16:51-08:00","id":1498795,"title":"","content":"Is there a list in the books or somewhere of the sources used for the pantheon write ups?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T01:10:31-08:00","id":1498826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1355712-scion-products\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1355712-scion-products\"> Scion Products - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1355712-scion-products\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1355712-scion-products </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> (2018-08-01) Storypath System Preview (2021): PDF from DriveThruRPG (https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/353047?affiliate_id=13&amp;amp;src=OPPForums) Merch from </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, missundersrood the question, but useful link, anyway\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-05-2022, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T13:42:03-08:00","id":1499678,"title":"","content":"Are there any rules or guidelines on creating new knacks? If so, where might I find them?<br /> <br /> Also, do relics allow you to have and use more boons than the base number a character has based on their Legend score? The Key of Saint Peter, for instance, provides the Scion with the Unbarred Passage Boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T14:01:40-08:00","id":1499682,"title":"","content":"Does Saints &amp; Monsters have new knacks for Scions in general or only for Titanic Scions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1487129#post1487129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you haven't already picked up Saints &amp; Monsters, it has a fair number of Immortal and Heroic Knacks specifically for Scions, so that ought to help you out there. It also includes guidance on Titanic Demigods, which can undergo Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T16:44:23-08:00","id":1499695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1499682#post1499682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Saints &amp; Monsters have new knacks for Scions in general or only for Titanic Scions?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>[since this is a question about the content of an already published book]<br /> <br /> Any Scion can take Titan Callings, it is just likely to get you distrusted. In addition to those five Callings, there are two other optional Callings in the book for Scions - Shepherd and Outsider. Now personally I harvested those Knacks for other Callings (mostly Guardian and Liminal respectively) rather than introduce those two new ones as a whole, but they\u2019re good Knacks!<br /> <br /> Also of course Denizen Scions are able to take the book\u2019s Denizen Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-14-2022, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T05:44:35-08:00","id":1500175,"title":"","content":"Possibly a dumb question, but the tv tropes entry says that dragons are the deities of the dinosaurs. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T23:22:42-08:00","id":1502735,"title":"","content":"A question; where is Scion going from here? Now God is done, there are a few releases in the art direction cue, which seem to be conneced to certain very specific things (wild hunt, possibly Arthurian/Welsh mythology), and which were announced some time ago. I'm not a fan of Dragon or Mythos as supplementary material (though obviously many others are), so those products won't get my dollars. And I will believe the TV show exists when I actually see it, given Hollywood's track record of unfulfilled promises - and that isn't a game supplement anyway. But where does the line go from here? Endless &quot;tasty bit&quot; additions? Or is there more in the wings we just don't know about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T03:32:57-07:00","id":1523616,"title":"","content":"Can a Scion be Born of a god, but be Chosen by another? For example, imagine someone is selected by God A to be their Chosen Scion, but the guy in question is already a pre-Visitation child of God B. Does that someone become a Chosen Scion of God A, with their original parentage overridden, or do they become a Born Scion of God B, their blood heritage taking priority?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T11:06:10-07:00","id":1523646,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not the line dev but since I did write an antagonist for Titans Rising who changed his Patron I\u2019m going to say it\u2019s a thing that can happen. I don\u2019t know if the details on what happens with callings and or the heritage stuff though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T04:14:13-07:00","id":1523765,"title":"","content":"bug\u00fcn nhh6h","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T09:28:57-08:00","id":1526114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1500175#post1500175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly a dumb question, but the tv tropes entry says that dragons are the deities of the dinosaurs. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware of anything in Scion 2e (published or unpublished) that treats dinosaurs as a sapient civilization that would have deities, let alone something that establishes Dragons as the Gods of them. <br /> <br /> Which is a long-winded way of saying &quot;No, and I have no idea where that idea came from.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:11:37-08:00","id":1526117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1502735#post1502735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question; where is Scion going from here? Now God is done, there are a few releases in the art direction cue, which seem to be conneced to certain very specific things (wild hunt, possibly Arthurian/Welsh mythology), and which were announced some time ago. I'm not a fan of Dragon or Mythos as supplementary material (though obviously many others are), so those products won't get my dollars. And I will believe the TV show exists when I actually see it, given Hollywood's track record of unfulfilled promises - and that isn't a game supplement anyway. But where does the line go from here? Endless &quot;tasty bit&quot; additions? Or is there more in the wings we just don't know about?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're spreading out in different ways of supporting and expanding Scion games. The recently-announced Rock Gods &amp; Side Quests gets into the idea of lower stakes games where the Scions are looking to succeed on a concert tour (or any other situation where Scions are traveling and solving problems instead of getting into big clashes with their enemies.) It also has a big chunk for playing mini-games when not all of the players can make it to that week's game.<br /> <br /> There are several other books in various states of progress that do similar things, providing frameworks for new adventures as well as supporting those that people are already playing (but house-ruling). Some of this support is going to come in the form of campaign-type books, like the long-awaited No Gods, No Monsters. Others are going to expand the World in terms of player options and problems, others are going to focus on providing more problems.<br /> <br /> And then there's the project that I can't talk about yet. It's going to provide a HUGE swath of player and game options. It's going to open up a lot of doors that people didn't even know were there. Those on Team Scion who know about the project are hyped, which is a great sign. I'll be talking more about it as it gets further along, especially since I'm about 80% sure it's going to be the next crowdfunded Scion book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:17:54-08:00","id":1526118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1526117#post1526117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're spreading out in different ways of supporting and expanding Scion games. The recently-announced Rock Gods &amp; Side Quests gets into the idea of lower stakes games where the Scions are looking to succeed on a concert tour (or any other situation where Scions are traveling and solving problems instead of getting into big clashes with their enemies.) It also has a big chunk for playing mini-games when not all of the players can make it to that week's game.<br /> <br /> There are several other books in various states of progress that do similar things, providing frameworks for new adventures as well as supporting those that people are already playing (but house-ruling). Some of this support is going to come in the form of campaign-type books, like the long-awaited No Gods, No Monsters. Others are going to expand the World in terms of player options and problems, others are going to focus on providing more problems.<br /> <br /> And then there's the project that I can't talk about yet. It's going to provide a HUGE swath of player and game options. It's going to open up a lot of doors that people didn't even know were there. Those on Team Scion who know about the project are hyped, which is a great sign. I'll be talking more about it as it gets further along, especially since I'm about 80% sure it's going to be the next crowdfunded Scion book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm SO HYPE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:24:22-08:00","id":1526119,"title":"","content":"Hiromi, I was actually curious on how two setting elements from Mage the Ascension could exist in Scion, <br /> could something similar to the One worshipped by the Celestial Chorus tradition exist in the World? And Could the Akashic Record of the Akashayana exist in the world?<br /> <br /> I actually asked about them before but I didn't note the answers down,sorry about repeating myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:49:06-08:00","id":1526123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1523616#post1523616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Scion be Born of a god, but be Chosen by another? For example, imagine someone is selected by God A to be their Chosen Scion, but the guy in question is already a pre-Visitation child of God B. Does that someone become a Chosen Scion of God A, with their original parentage overridden, or do they become a Born Scion of God B, their blood heritage taking priority?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are valid options. We don't have mechanics set up to make a concrete ruling because that's something that would be better played out through RP. That's not to say that we won't even make mechanics, but I think it's probably best to leave it in players' hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:49:56-08:00","id":1526124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1523765#post1523765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bug\u00fcn nhh6h</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello Hermeticus' cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:58:26-08:00","id":1526125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1526119#post1526119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiromi, I was actually curious on how two setting elements from Mage the Ascension could exist in Scion,<br /> could something similar to the One worshipped by the Celestial Chorus tradition exist in the World? And Could the Akashic Record of the Akashayana exist in the world?<br /> <br /> I actually asked about them before but I didn't note the answers down,sorry about repeating myself</div> </div> </div> </div>The One could easily exist as a deity in the World. I don't think Onyx Path has the rights to create such a deity, and creating monotheistic pantheons is against the Storypath Nexus' rules, so I wouldn't expect much support for that idea.<br /> <br /> The Akashic Record could also exist in the World. I think treating it as a Guide would make the most sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T14:13:04-08:00","id":1526133,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T19:35:47-08:00","id":1526220,"title":"","content":"Why was the name &quot;Palas&quot; chosen to refer to the Buddhist pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T08:33:27-08:00","id":1526232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayNg2183</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1526220#post1526220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was the name &quot;Palas&quot; chosen to refer to the Buddhist pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>P\u0101la is Pali and Sanskrit for \u201cguardian&quot; or &quot;protector.&quot; In Buddhism, the word is more common as a compound word than on its own (e.g. Lokap\u0101las &amp; Dharmap\u0101las, protectors of the world &amp; the dharma, respectively). Some schools of Buddhism collect all of the protector deities and spirits under Dharmap\u0101las, with Lokap\u0101las being a subcategory, but that's not a universally agreed upon taxonomy. So, to get all of the deities under a single umbrella, we went with P\u0101las instead of a more specific category.<br /> <br /> There's a snippet at the end of the introduction to the P\u0101las that briefly explains the meaning of &quot;p\u0101las,&quot; but it's possible that you missed it because it glosses &quot;p\u0101la,&quot; the singular form instead of &quot;p\u0101las,&quot; the plural form in English. The book is far enough down the pipeline that I might not be able to do anything about that, but I'll look into tweaking the wording to cause folks less confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A deity who practices this meritorious and profound teaching of the<br /> Buddha will become a protector of the Buddhist Way.\u201d<br /> In P\u0101li and Sanskrit, the term for such a protector is \u201cp\u0101la.\u201d\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making TTRPGs queerer and more culturally diverse since 2016","edited":{"userid":27136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","user":"Hiromi","date":". 12-04-2023, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27136-hiromi","name":"Hiromi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T23:33:39-08:00","id":1526267,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T14:41:41-08:00","id":1526372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1526232#post1526232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P\u0101la is Pali and Sanskrit for \u201cguardian&quot; or &quot;protector.&quot; In Buddhism, the word is more common as a compound word than on its own (e.g. Lokap\u0101las &amp; Dharmap\u0101las, protectors of the world &amp; the dharma, respectively). Some schools of Buddhism collect all of the protector deities and spirits under Dharmap\u0101las, with Lokap\u0101las being a subcategory, but that's not a universally agreed upon taxonomy. So, to get all of the deities under a single umbrella, we went with P\u0101las instead of a more specific category.<br /> <br /> There's a snippet at the end of the introduction to the P\u0101las that briefly explains the meaning of &quot;p\u0101las,&quot; but it's possible that you missed it because it glosses &quot;p\u0101la,&quot; the singular form instead of &quot;p\u0101las,&quot; the plural form in English. The book is far enough down the pipeline that I might not be able to do anything about that, but I'll look into tweaking the wording to cause folks less confusion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know the ship has long since sailed on this, but another option could have been the Mahasattvas, literally &quot;Great Beings.&quot; It's used as a synonym for Bodhisattva, but it seems like something that could have been used in a more expansive sense in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T14:44:47-08:00","id":1526373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hiromi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1464547-ask-the-line-dev?p=1526117#post1526117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're spreading out in different ways of supporting and expanding Scion games. The recently-announced Rock Gods &amp; Side Quests gets into the idea of lower stakes games where the Scions are looking to succeed on a concert tour (or any other situation where Scions are traveling and solving problems instead of getting into big clashes with their enemies.) It also has a big chunk for playing mini-games when not all of the players can make it to that week's game.<br /> <br /> There are several other books in various states of progress that do similar things, providing frameworks for new adventures as well as supporting those that people are already playing (but house-ruling). Some of this support is going to come in the form of campaign-type books, like the long-awaited No Gods, No Monsters. Others are going to expand the World in terms of player options and problems, others are going to focus on providing more problems.<br /> <br /> And then there's the project that I can't talk about yet. It's going to provide a HUGE swath of player and game options. It's going to open up a lot of doors that people didn't even know were there. Those on Team Scion who know about the project are hyped, which is a great sign. I'll be talking more about it as it gets further along, especially since I'm about 80% sure it's going to be the next crowdfunded Scion book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there plans for more pantheons? Or do you feel like the possibilities in terms of doing something new and different in that regard have been exhausted? The pantheon write-ups are one of my favorite parts of Scion, so I would like to see more--but I can understand if that doesn't make sense from the production side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T07:58:45-08:00","id":1526705,"title":"","content":"Are you in liberty of telling us more about Mythic Shards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T18:07:09-07:00","id":1540867,"title":"","content":"can god-tier player characters buy more knacks than the ones they already have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T12:48:55-07:00","id":1542515,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for non-Plant Don Scions to end up with Arthurian Fatebound roles and Mantles? And should Arthurian Mantles complete Apotheosis, would they join the Plant Don or would it create its own separate Arthurian Pantheon? Can Scions change Pantheons?<br /> <br /> Unrelated second question: can Primordials have their own Scions?<br /> <br /> EDIT: third question: would Alesia have particular importance to the Nemetondevos, as the site of the last stand of the Gauls? Could Vercingetorix have been a Gaulish Scion, and if so, of which God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 09-26-2024, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T17:11:04-07:00","id":1550612,"title":"","content":"In the Scion: Demigod Companion, we're presented with the Dominion Boons for the 5 Signature Purviews of the Pantheons presented in Scion: Demigod, but I can't find a single place where the Dominion Boons are presented for any of the other Signature Purviews for the Pantheons from Hero. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}